spec: specs/sql.md "The brake runs on a failing statement" (Results)

why: guardAsync in Resource.run held a row cast outside the kernel
  (<|> is the one trusted place); the operator asked for the typeclass
  route if nothing better exists — and the probe showed dotty resolves
  Async-anchored union instances, so the cast disappears entirely.

what: core Failing[F] — how a forwarded operation of F reports failure
  to the scope that forwarded it: Async's instance is a typed GADT
  match, the row instances split by Async's own TypeableK through <|>
  and upcast back, a low-priority plain instance for rows without
  Async; Resource.run takes (using Failing[F]); guardAsync deleted.

